Angels are gods too.  They're just lesser gods that monotheists don't feel
comfortable accepting as gods. Saints would be demigods. In most religions
(present day) angels are not creative gods, and they are subserviant to
another god.

The use of "Elbereth" in Nethack seems to be using a word of power derived
from a [semi]divine individual.  Much like "Abracadabra" derives from
Abraxis, an archon from gnostic cosmology. Whether the power is
supernatural, preternatural, or some other nature I couldn't really say.

